`find_embeddings(root, label, view, subjects=None)` returns a label's recording files, found on disk with MNE-BIDS, never through a manifest. `load_embeddings` reads one or several embedding files into a float32 `DataContainer`, one row per window or, with `representation="recording"`, per recording and condition, and reads only the windows of the requested `conditions` and `subjects`; it refuses files that differ in model, settings, label, view or channels, a requested condition no file holds, an observation seen twice and non-finite values. Its rows are named as the BIDS loader's, so an epoch and the embedding extracted from it share an ID. `consolidate_embeddings` writes recordings' files as one file at the dataset root, one recording at a time. `EmbeddingConfig` now takes `path`, `representation`, `conditions`, `subjects` and `aggregate_by`, `load_data` reads it with `load_embeddings`, and `report.from_embeddings` reads an embedding file. `EmbeddingConfig.subjects` takes subject labels; a number no longer loads the first files. Removed: `EmbeddingDataset`, `smart_reader`, the `pattern`, `dims` and `coords` fields of `EmbeddingConfig`, and `load_data`'s `reader` and `id_fn` arguments.
